-- title:
--   Diamond automorphisms at levels M and M/p agree
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $M$ a nonzero natural number with $p \mid M$, and $H$ a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$. Write $E =$ `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` for the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ generated by the image, under the coefficientwise embedding of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ into $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$, of the $q$-expansion function field `xHFunctionFieldC ℚ M H` of $\Gamma_H(M)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$; write $E'$ for the corresponding field at level $M/p$ with the subgroup `infSubgroup p M H hpM`, namely the image of $H$ under the reduction map $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$. For $d \in (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$, `diamondAutHBar M H d` is the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra automorphism of $E$ chosen to satisfy the predicate `IsDiamondAutHBar M H d` — that for all $k$, all modular forms $f, g$ of weight $k$ on $\Gamma_H(M)$ with integral $q$-expansions and $g \ne 0$, and all $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M)$ whose upper-left entry reduces to $d$ mod $M$, the image of $f/g$ is the embedding of an element $y$ of the rational function field with $y \cdot (g \mid_k \gamma) = f \mid_k \gamma$ as $q$-expansions over $\mathbb{C}$ — and is the identity if no such automorphism exists. The assertion: if $x \in E$ and $u \in E'$ have the same underlying Laurent series in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$, then `diamondAutHBar M H d x` and `diamondAutHBar (M / p) (infSubgroup p M H hpM) d' u`, where $d'$ is the image of $d$ under the reduction map attached to $(M/p) \mid M$, again have the same underlying Laurent series.
--
--   This is the compatibility of the diamond operators with the inclusion of the level-$M/p$ function field into the level-$M$ one: $\langle d \rangle$ at level $M$ restricts to $\langle \bar{d} \rangle$ at level $M/p$, both being induced by $f/g \mapsto (f\mid\gamma)/(g\mid\gamma)$ for a single $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M) \subseteq \Gamma_0(M/p)$. It is used in the comparison of the de Rham models at $p$ for the two levels, and in the statements that the diamond automorphisms commute with the level-changing maps.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_coe_diamondAutHBar_eq_coe_diamondAutHBar_div_of_coe_eq.lean

